{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Heavy Rental Spring REST API",
    "description": "Manual API tests for `heavy-rental-spring-rest-api` (port 8080).\n\n## Auth flow (required for most routes)\n1. Run **Auth → 1. Get interim Bearer token** — saves `interimToken`.\n2. Run **Auth → 2. Login** — saves `accessToken` (Bearer for other folders).\n3. Run protected requests (collection auth uses `{{accessToken}}`).\n\n## Seed users (local / data.sql)\n| Email | Password | Role |\n|-------|----------|------|\n| admin@localhost | admin1234 | ADMIN |\n| alex.tan@example.sg | customer123 | USER (has an active QUOTED plan `3` — `POST /rentalPlans` → 409) |\n| mei.lin@example.sg | customer456 | USER (no plans — use for cart → quote → checkout) |\n\n## Rental plans + checkout\n1. Login as **Mei Lin** (or re-quote Alex Tan plan `3` first).\n2. **Rental Plans → Create** → add item → quote. Saves `rentalPlanId`.\n3. **Bookings → Checkout from rental plan** — `rentalPlanId` only; items/dates ignored.\n4. `409 quote_expired` → re-run **Request quote**, then checkout again.\n5. `siteAddress` MUST end with a 6-digit postal code (`400 validation_failed` otherwise).\n\n## Recommender (S2b)\n- `POST /project-spec` → Call 1 ingest + Call 2 recommend quote (`quoteRef`, `items`).\n- `POST .../knowledge-query` → Call 3 chatbot (`answer`, `sourcesUsed`).\n- Requires haystack at `haystack.base-url` (default `http://localhost:8000`).\n\nSee OpenSpec `openspec/specs/api-index/contracts/routes.md`, `openspec/specs/rental-plan-quote/contracts/checkout.md`, and `openspec/specs/haystack-recommender/`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "interimToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "alex.tan@example.sg" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "customer123" },
    { "key": "recommendationId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "bookingId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "rentalPlanId", "value": "3" },
    { "key": "rentalPlanItemId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "equipmentId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "correlationId", "value": "postman-corr-001" },
    { "key": "googleIdToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "postalCode", "value": "619094" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Actuator health",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health",
            "description": "Public liveness. No JWT required."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Two-step JWT: interim (public) → login/google (ROLE_INTERIM) → access token (ROLE_USER/ADMIN/DRIVER). `POST /api/auth/google` is the mobile ops app's sign-in path and only ever provisions `ROLE_DRIVER` accounts.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Get interim Bearer token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const token = pm.response.text().trim();",
                  "pm.test('Body is non-empty JWT text', () => pm.expect(token.length).to.be.above(20));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('interimToken', token);",
                  "console.log('interimToken saved (length ' + token.length + ')');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "text/plain" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/getBearerToken",
            "description": "Public. Returns plain-text interim JWT (no `Bearer` prefix). Test script stores it as `interimToken`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has accessToken', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "console.log('accessToken saved; username=' + body.username);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{interimToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
            "description": "Requires interim Bearer. Body: email + password. Saves `accessToken` for collection auth."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2b. Login with Google (mobile)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has accessToken', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "console.log('accessToken saved; username=' + body.username);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{interimToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idToken\": \"{{googleIdToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google",
            "description": "Mobile ops app only — alternative to Login using a Google ID token instead of a password. Requires interim Bearer. Set collection variable `googleIdToken` to a real Google-issued ID token (from Android Credential Manager) before running — there is no way to obtain one from Postman itself. First-time sign-in auto-provisions a `ROLE_DRIVER` account; an existing account keeps its current role."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', '');",
                  "console.log('accessToken cleared after logout');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
            "description": "Revokes current access token. Uses collection Bearer `{{accessToken}}`. Re-login after this."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Recommendations (S2b)",
      "description": "Portal recommender. Needs access JWT + running haystack for submit/query.\n\nSubmit response is Call 2 **quote** (`quoteRef`, `items`) — not Call 3 `answer`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit project-spec (Call 1 + Call 2 quote)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.recommendationId != null) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('recommendationId', String(body.recommendationId));",
                  "  console.log('recommendationId=' + body.recommendationId + ' ingestId=' + body.ingestId + ' quoteRef=' + body.quoteRef);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Has recommendationId and ingestId', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.recommendationId).to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.ingestId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Primary body is quote (not chatbot answer)', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('quoteRef');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('items');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('answer');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Correlation-Id", "value": "{{correlationId}}", "description": "Optional; propagated to haystack" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"projectText\": \"Foundation excavation at Marina South. Need excavator and dump truck for 10 days. Soft soil, 4m depth. Site access via B2 ramp.\",\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-09-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-09-12\",\n  \"userName\": \"Alex Tan\",\n  \"query\": null,\n  \"topK\": 5\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/project-spec",
            "description": "Orchestrates haystack Call 1 then Call 2 recommend. Saves `recommendationId` on success.\n\nResponse includes session fields + `quoteRef`, `items`, rates — **not** `answer`/`sourcesUsed`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit project-spec (multipart file)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.recommendationId != null) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('recommendationId', String(body.recommendationId));",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Has quoteRef', () => pm.expect(body.quoteRef).to.exist);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Correlation-Id", "value": "{{correlationId}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select a small .txt/.pdf project-spec file"
                },
                {
                  "key": "projectText",
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Optional caption alongside file",
                  "description": "Optional if file is present"
                },
                { "key": "topK", "type": "text", "value": "5" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/project-spec",
            "description": "Multipart Call 1 (file and/or projectText) then Call 2 quote. Max size: haystack.max-in-memory-size (20MB default)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Knowledge query (Call 3 chatbot)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has chatbot answer', () => pm.expect(body.answer).to.exist);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"query\": \"What working height or capacity constraints apply to this project?\",\n  \"topK\": 5\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/{{recommendationId}}/knowledge-query",
            "description": "Call 3 only — uses stored `ingest_id`. Returns `answer` / `sourcesUsed`. Does not re-ingest."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get recommendation session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has session fields', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.recommendationId).to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.ingestId).to.exist;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/recommendations/{{recommendationId}}",
            "description": "DB-only session summary. No haystack call. Owner or admin."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Assets (web)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Browse assets",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets?category=&search=&condition=&startDate=&endDate=",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "assets"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "category", "value": "", "description": "Optional category filter", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "search", "value": "", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "condition", "value": "", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "startDate", "value": "2026-09-01", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "endDate", "value": "2026-09-12", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "List assets. Optional query: category, search, condition, startDate, endDate. Open to any authenticated user."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get asset by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets/{{equipmentId}}",
            "description": "Single asset by id. Open to any authenticated user."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create asset (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Excavator\",\n  \"serialno\": \"PM-EX-001\",\n  \"categoryId\": 1,\n  \"baseDailyRate\": 450.00,\n  \"minDailyRate\": 400.00,\n  \"maxDailyRate\": 550.00,\n  \"capacity\": 20,\n  \"platformHeight\": null,\n  \"purchaseYear\": 2022,\n  \"condition\": \"GOOD\",\n  \"desc\": \"Created from Postman collection\",\n  \"location\": \"Tuas Depot\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets",
            "description": "Create asset. Adjust `categoryId` / `condition` to match seed enums. Requires a ROLE_ADMIN access token — a ROLE_USER token gets 403."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update asset (PUT, admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Excavator (updated)\",\n  \"serialno\": \"PM-EX-001\",\n  \"categoryId\": 1,\n  \"baseDailyRate\": 460.00,\n  \"minDailyRate\": 400.00,\n  \"maxDailyRate\": 560.00,\n  \"capacity\": 20,\n  \"platformHeight\": null,\n  \"purchaseYear\": 2022,\n  \"condition\": \"GOOD\",\n  \"desc\": \"Updated from Postman\",\n  \"location\": \"Tuas Depot\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets/{{equipmentId}}",
            "description": "Full replace of asset fields. Requires a ROLE_ADMIN access token — a ROLE_USER token gets 403."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Patch asset (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Excavator (patched)\",\n  \"serialno\": null,\n  \"categoryId\": null,\n  \"baseDailyRate\": 470.00,\n  \"minDailyRate\": null,\n  \"maxDailyRate\": null,\n  \"capacity\": null,\n  \"platformHeight\": null,\n  \"purchaseYear\": null,\n  \"condition\": null,\n  \"desc\": null,\n  \"location\": null\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets/{{equipmentId}}",
            "description": "Partial update (same request type as create; null fields are left unchanged). Requires a ROLE_ADMIN access token — a ROLE_USER token gets 403."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload asset image (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"image\": \"<raw base64, no data: prefix>\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets/{{equipmentId}}/image",
            "description": "Replace the asset's photo (at most one photo is kept per asset). Requires a ROLE_ADMIN access token — a ROLE_USER token gets 403. 413 if the base64 payload exceeds ~7,000,000 characters."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete asset (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/assets/{{equipmentId}}",
            "description": "Delete asset by id. Prefer a non-seeded id created via Create. Requires a ROLE_ADMIN access token — a ROLE_USER token gets 403."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Bookings (mobile)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create booking",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (body.id != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('bookingId', String(body.id));",
                  "  if (body.bookingId != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('bookingId', String(body.bookingId));",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [{ \"assetId\": 1 }],\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-10-10\",\n  \"siteAddress\": \"20 Jurong Port Road, 619094\",\n  \"deliveryNotes\": \"Call site contact 30 min before arrival\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/bookings",
            "description": "Direct booking (no `rentalPlanId`). Prices with inclusive days (`end − start + 1`). `siteAddress` MUST end with a 6-digit postal code. May 409 if the asset overlaps an active booking."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Checkout from rental plan",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (body.bookingId != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('bookingId', String(body.bookingId));",
                  "  if (body.id != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('bookingId', String(body.id));",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 409) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  console.log('checkout 409 error=' + body.error + ' message=' + body.message);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"rentalPlanId\": {{rentalPlanId}},\n  \"siteAddress\": \"20 Jurong Port Road, 619094\",\n  \"deliveryNotes\": \"Checkout from quoted plan\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/bookings",
            "description": "Plan-backed checkout (HR-140). Plan must be `QUOTED` and `updatedAt` within 24h.\n\n- `items`/`startDate`/`endDate` are ignored — derived from the plan.\n- Success: booking `PENDING_DEPOSIT`, plan → `CONVERTED` (saves `bookingId`).\n- `404` plan missing or not yours.\n- `409 quote_not_ready` if not QUOTED.\n- `409 quote_expired` if quote older than 24h — run **Rental Plans → Request quote**, then retry.\n- Seeded Alex Tan plan `3` is QUOTED but likely stale; re-quote first, or walk create→item→quote as Mei Lin."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List bookings",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/bookings",
            "description": "List bookings."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get booking by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}",
            "description": "Single booking."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update booking",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-10-02\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-10-12\",\n  \"siteAddress\": \"20 Jurong Port Road, 619094\",\n  \"deliveryNotes\": \"Updated notes from Postman\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}",
            "description": "Full-replace PUT of dates/site/notes. Does not change status. `siteAddress` MUST end with a 6-digit postal code."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Deliveries & Returns",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List deliveries",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Patch delivery status",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bookingStatus\": \"MOBILISED\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{bookingId}}/status",
            "description": "Only legal transition: current `CONFIRMED` → `MOBILISED`. Other pairs → 400."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List returns",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/returns"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Patch return status",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bookingStatus\": \"COMPLETED\",\n  \"returnNotes\": \"Returned from Postman\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/returns/{{bookingId}}/status",
            "description": "Only legal transition: `MOBILISED` → `COMPLETED`. Optional `returnNotes`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Payments",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create deposit intent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bookingId\": {{bookingId}}\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payments/deposit-intent",
            "description": "Creates Stripe PaymentIntent for booking deposit. Needs real `STRIPE_API_KEY` or fails on placeholder."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Stripe webhook (stub)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Stripe-Signature", "value": "t=0,v1=invalid-for-manual-test" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"evt_postman_test\",\n  \"type\": \"payment_intent.succeeded\",\n  \"data\": { \"object\": { \"id\": \"pi_test\" } }\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payments/webhook",
            "description": "Public path; signature verified with `stripe.webhook.secret`. Manual calls usually 400 unless you craft a valid Stripe signature."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Rental Plans",
      "description": "As-built `/api/rentalPlans` (camelCase). Ownership-scoped (`404` not `403`).\n\nWalk (prefer **mei.lin@example.sg** / `customer456`): Create → Add item → Request quote → Bookings → Checkout from rental plan.\n\nAlex Tan already has an active QUOTED plan (`3`), so Create → 409 until it's converted or cancelled. Either run **Request quote** (refresh `updatedAt`) then checkout, or **Cancel plan** to free the one-active-plan slot and Create a fresh one. Plans `2` and `6` are seeded `CANCELLED` for reference.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create plan",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (body.id != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('rentalPlanId', String(body.id));",
                  "  console.log('rentalPlanId=' + body.id + ' status=' + body.status);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-11-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-11-05\",\n  \"siteAddress\": \"20 Jurong Port Road, 619094\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans",
            "description": "`201 DRAFT`. One active plan (DRAFT/SAVED/QUOTED) per customer — second create → `409`. `siteAddress` is optional (the \"Skip for now\" cart flow) — omit it or send `null` to create with no address; WHEN provided it MUST end with a 6-digit postal code (`400 validation_failed`). See **Update site address** below for setting it later. Saves `rentalPlanId`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List my plans",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans",
            "description": "Caller's plans only. Includes `createdAt`/`updatedAt`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get plan by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}",
            "description": "Owner or `404`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Add item",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (body.items && body.items.length) {",
                  "    const last = body.items[body.items.length - 1];",
                  "    if (last.id != null) pm.collectionVariables.set('rentalPlanItemId', String(last.id));",
                  "  }",
                  "  console.log('plan status=' + body.status + ' totalAmount=' + body.totalAmount);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"assetId\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}/items",
            "description": "Snapshots `Asset.baseDailyRate`. On a `QUOTED` plan this succeeds and reverts status to `DRAFT` (`totalAmount` null). Saves `rentalPlanItemId`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove item",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}/items/{{rentalPlanItemId}}",
            "description": "Same revert-to-`DRAFT` behavior if the plan was `QUOTED`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update site address",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"siteAddress\": \"20 Jurong Port Road, 619094\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}",
            "description": "Sets/changes `siteAddress` on a plan created without one (the \"Skip for now\" flow) or corrects an existing one. `siteAddress` MUST end with a 6-digit postal code or omit/`null` to clear it (`400 validation_failed` if present but malformed). On a `QUOTED` plan this reverts status to `DRAFT` and clears `totalAmount` (the frozen total was priced using the old address's distance). `CONVERTED`/`CANCELLED` → `409`. Non-owner → `404`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Request quote",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  console.log('quoted totalAmount=' + body.totalAmount + ' updatedAt=' + body.updatedAt);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}/quote",
            "description": "Spring-only sum of line subtotals. Sets `QUOTED` and refreshes `updatedAt` (24h checkout window). Re-quote of `QUOTED` is allowed. Empty plan → 400. `CONVERTED` → 409. Then run **Bookings → Checkout from rental plan**."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel plan",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  console.log('plan status=' + body.status + ' totalAmount=' + body.totalAmount);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rentalPlans/{{rentalPlanId}}/cancel",
            "description": "Sets `CANCELLED`, clears `totalAmount`, refreshes `updatedAt`. Allowed from `DRAFT`/`SAVED`/`QUOTED`. `CONVERTED` → `409 already_converted`; already `CANCELLED` → `409 already_cancelled`. `CANCELLED` does not count toward the one-active-plan rule, so **Create plan** works again afterward."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Stubs (web)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List depots (stub)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/depots",
            "description": "Always returns `[]` — stub for React portal. Rental plans are real under folder 7 (`/api/rentalPlans`)."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Postal Codes",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validate postal code",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/postalCodes/{{postalCode}}",
            "description": "Real-time postal code validation (pricing-postal-distance). 200 with status VALID/INVALID, or 503 with status UNAVAILABLE if OneMap itself is down — see openspec/changes/pricing-postal-distance/contracts/postal-code-validation.md. Set {{postalCode}} to a malformed value (e.g. 12345) to see the 400 case instead."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
